aqueousThermo
{
source "hfAq [kJ/mol] -408.78: printed dfH(aq) His- -97.70 kcal/mol x 4.184 -- Amend & Helgeson, Calculation of the standard molal thermodynamic properties of aqueous biomolecules at elevated temperatures and pressures. Part 1. L-alpha-Amino acids, J. Chem. Soc., Faraday Trans. 93 (1997) 1927-1941, Table 1, p. 1929, row His-, Amend & Helgeson state this value as calculated from the crystal's formation enthalpy and heat of solution (neutral) or from the neutral and the printed ionisation enthalpy (charged), Table 1 footnotes d-s ## sAq [J/mol/K] 245.85: printed S His- 58.76 cal/mol/K x 4.184 -- Amend & Helgeson, Calculation of the standard molal thermodynamic properties of aqueous biomolecules at elevated temperatures and pressures. Part 1. L-alpha-Amino acids, J. Chem. Soc., Faraday Trans. 93 (1997) 1927-1941, Table 1, p. 1929, row His-, calculated by the authors from the printed DfG and DfH with the elements' entropies (Table 1 footnote c), H+ = 0";
